{"annotationDigest":"sha256:fc1597573141d1d13393515f49980d9520051b3885f89582c224f8ad80048892","annotationId":"rann-4b398df3ce67583e856ffa1e63c6c630","author":{"agent":"claude-code","kind":"ai","model":"claude-opus-5.5"},"createdAt":"2026-10-02T00:18:23Z","disclaimer":"AI-generated review opinion derived from the evidence package. It is not a verdict, does not change readiness, and must be confirmed by a human reviewer.","disclosureCheck":{"blocking":7,"contradictions":[],"disclosures":10,"nextDecision":"human_judgement","readiness":"not_assessed"},"findings":[{"claim":{"params":{"requirement":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2"},"type":"requirement_affected"},"detail":"Function-level trace on stripJsonc and parseMenuJsonc. The requirement text still says 'strips full-line // comments'; the PR widens this to any // outside a string. The wording is not amended on this mirror (only the trace review was restamped), so the spec now under-describes the code: consider rewording E4J2.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":8},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2 (JSONC stripping) is code_changed: stripJsonc is rewritten as a string-aware scanner","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2","kind":"requirement"}],"method":"review.changes (spec, code-trace, function and call-level requirement impact)","note":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2 is in review.changes (code_changed, matchLevel function).","status":"confirmed"}},{"claim":{"params":{"requirement":"SW-REQ-260922-3T3F"},"type":"requirement_affected"},"detail":"parseMenuJsonc still returns [] on a JSON.parse failure and no exception escapes; the PR adds a guarded console.warn in the catch (MenuModel.js:82-83). Both arms of the guard are pinned by the replay test (menumodel-replay.test.mjs:1048-1062).","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":82},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-3T3F","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"