. The scanner deletes only the comment and copies the indent; JSON.parse accepts only space/tab/LF/CR, so VT, FF, U+00A0, U+1680, U+2000-U+200A, U+2028, U+2029, U+202F, U+205F, U+3000 or U+FEFF indenting a comment line empties the whole file (0 rows + the new warning). I re-ran base vs head MenuModel.js in node: base 2 rows, head 0 for all 12 sampled chars; tab/space unaffected. pocs/pr6525-comment-indent-whitespace.sh is a green tripwire (21/21 chars, exit 0). This is cf-39627352fe66ab9c (removed_behavior, unapproved), introduced by the PR's mirror commit dff129dc; it violates E4J2 on that partition. Quickshell's FileView drops a LEADING BOM, so a BOM at the very start of the file does not trigger it under the shell (recorded live in the KI, Quickshell 0.3.1; not re-checked here); the same characters on any later comment line do. Remedy: copy JS whitespace outside strings as a space (as #13968 b2dae8db does).","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":25},{"id":"pocs/pr6525-comment-indent-whitespace.sh","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-JSONC-COMMENT-INDENT-WHITESPACE.yaml","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Regression (KI-MENU-JSONC-COMMENT-INDENT-WHITESPACE): does a whole-line comment indented with non-JSON JS whitespace still parse?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Comment-lines-only Unicode indent partition\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"detail":"review.behaviorDiff ran 213 inputs (data 176) and recorded only the 2 intended corpus differences. The builtin_data generator puts each JS \\s character at the start of the file or before EVERY line; all three seeds start with `{` and every line carries tokens, so base and head both fail JSON.parse (I reproduced: every-line and file-start variants give 0 rows at base and head). No partition puts the character ONLY before comment lines, so the differential is silent; the regression was found by the removed_behavior inventory and the baseline's E4J2 witness. Suggest a comment-lines-only data mode in the generator.","refs":[{"id":"test/bdiff/harness.mjs","kind":"file","line":69},{"id":"proof.yaml","kind":"file","line":546},{"id":"review.behaviorDiff","kind":"check"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Process note: the configured behaviour-diff harness did not catch this regression","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"test_diff reports only the two node test files. In test/shell.d/menu-test.sh the baseline's `SW-REQ-260922-E4J2:input_domain:nominal` witness (expects 'a=A|b=B' for a comment indented with NBSP/U+3000/VT/FF/BOM/U+2028) now expects '' and lost its obligation tag (lines 273-283, proof work in e16420ab, deliberately turned into the regression's tripwire), and the two INLINE-COMMENT tripwires flipped 0 to 1/2 rows (241-251). The first is a weakened guarantee test a human should see as a compat change; the engine did not surface it.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-test.sh","kind":"file","line":278},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-test.sh","kind":"file","line":241},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Process note: compat test_diff did not flag the changed menu-test.sh witnesses","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"With /m, ^ also matched after \\r, U+2028, U+2029. My node runs: a comment after CR-only line ends or after U+2028 gives the same rows at base and head (0 in both; CR-only files stay broken, KI-MENU-JSONC-CR-LINE-ENDINGS). The only observed difference from the anchors is the whitespace-indent case of finding 4. Unapproved: a human reviewer must accept it.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":25},{"id":"review.compat","kind":"check"}],"severity":"low","title":"Compat cf-06aced0efb52f0f2 (removed m-flag anchors): preserved in effect apart from finding 4","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"Both are dogfood proof work (commit e16420ab), not the upstream PR. Report #13493's test now expects exit 0; it was flagged 'deleted' because the test was renamed, its control assertion is still present (report-reproducers.test.mjs:53). The regex-era stripJsonc MC/DC replay block is replaced by one covering the scanner's decisions and the new warn guard (menumodel-replay.test.mjs:1018-1062). Auditor notes exist; they are not approvals.","refs":[{"id":"test/node/report-reproducers.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":50},{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1018}],"severity":"info","title":"Compat cf-2f1169dc59e4e167 and cf-c3bc89d90b0bed0a (test_diff): proof-side test edits, intended, unapproved","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"`out.replace(/,(\\s*[}\\]])/g, \"$1\")` at MenuModel.js:34 is byte-identical to the base second pass. It still also rewrites `,}` inside strings (KI-MENU-JSONC-COMMA-IN-STRING stays open; I reproduced 'x ,}' becoming 'x }' at base and head).","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":34},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-test.sh","kind":"file","line":1}],"severity":"info","title":"Compat cf-dc379a6ee10eec0f (comma regex \\s): fixed, the comma pass is unchanged and preserved by menu-tes