itespace.sh","path":"pocs/pr6525-comment-indent-whitespace.sh","position":"intended"},"type":"unmapped_code"},"detail":"The file is dogfood proof work (e16420ab), not part of omacom/omarchy#6525. It is the green tripwire of KI-MENU-JSONC-COMMENT-INDENT-WHITESPACE: `# Reproduces:` marker, the KI's reproducer_command and evidence, and the KI's affected requirement SW-REQ-260922-E4J2 already codify why it exists. It adds no product behaviour, so the candidate is an analyzer false positive for pocs/ reproducers (the fix is to let a Reproduces: marker count as intent, or exclude pocs/ from unmapped-code scope), not a missing requirement.","refs":[{"id":"pocs/pr6525-comment-indent-whitespace.sh","kind":"file","line":2},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-JSONC-COMMENT-INDENT-WHITESPACE.yaml","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Unmapped pocs/pr6525-comment-indent-whitespace.sh is our audit reproducer, not PR behaviour","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"unmapped_code|pocs/pr6525-comment-indent-whitespace.sh","kind":"candidate"},{"id":"pocs/pr6525-comment-indent-whitespace.sh","kind":"file"}],"method":"review.scope (changed units, intent graph, spec-gap candidates): specGapCandidates","note":"The package flags unmapped_code|pocs/pr6525-comment-indent-whitespace.sh (unmapped_code, severity medium): New file pocs/pr6525-comment-indent-whitespace.sh is traced to no requirement: behaviour without intent. The author's position (intended) is judgement, not verified; a human decision settles it.","status":"confirmed"}},{"detail":"Verified in node at base and head: an inline tail parses (0 to 1 row); `,}` in a string is still rewritten; non-JSON whitespace between tokens and CR-only comment files still give 0 rows; /* */ still gives 0 rows (the PR documents it as unsupported, and the new warning now at least logs it). Array root is untouched by the diff (parseMenuJsonc's type check is unchanged).","refs":[{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-JSONC-INLINE-COMMENT.yaml","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-JSONC-STRIP-GAPS.yaml","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":84}],"severity":"info","title":"KI-MENU-JSONC-INLINE-COMMENT fixed; COMMA-IN-STRING, ARRAY-ROOT, UNICODE-WHITESPACE, CR-LINE-ENDINGS, STRIP-GAPS stay open","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"dff129dc = the upstream PR (913e112d) applied on quattro-proof 9f3abc10: MenuModel.js scanner + warn, docs/menu.md, one menu-test.sh hunk (lines 66-73, identical to the PR). e16420ab..ac92b864 = our proof work: witness/tripwire edits, the pocs script, KI filing (INLINE-COMMENT fixed, COMMENT-INDENT-WHITESPACE new), trace re-review, KI evidence.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-test.sh","kind":"file","line":66}],"severity":"info","title":"Mirror composition: upstream change vs dogfood proof work","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"decisionSummary discloses effects_unavailable (no review.effects for this JS/QML project), so no new_call_path / effect_gain claims are possible. Read by hand: the only new callee is console.warn in parseMenuJsonc's catch; callers are Menu.qml:1044 (default menu) and :1055 (user extension) via FileView onLoaded. 14 checks were skipped by configuration (checks_skipped).","refs":[{"id":"review.effects.approximations","kind":"check"},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":1055}],"severity":"info","title":"Change effects not analyzed; analysis bounds acknowledged","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js:parseMenuJsonc"],"scenario":"in a running Quickshell, load the shipped default menu and a user extension with an inline // tail and a malformed line through Menu.qml FileView: same rows as node, and one 'MenuModel: failed to parse' line in the shell log for the malformed file"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"All runtime evidence here is node. The per-character string concatenation and console.warn inside QML JS are not observed in the shell; menu-compositor/acceptance tests are live Hyprland/Quickshell tests in no audit suite.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":1044},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-3T3F","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: does the scanner and the console.warn behave the same under Quickshell's QV4 as under node?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"QV4 witness: inline-comment and malformed user extension inside Quickshell\".","status":"needs_test"}}],"packageDigest":"sha256:25966a33b810cbf865a0c699995d6b5cd13b0f35b8de639e99d77728b03bde4d","packageIdentity":"epkg-1105e5ad3f8467374895c8d1c6d9259fb1464b070944994ef4df310853270796","riskAssessment":{"level":"medium","rationale":"The purpose is fixed and exercised, but the PR introduces a recorded regression (a comment line indented with non-JSON whitespace empties the menu file) that the differential harness missed, and six compatibility changes await human approval."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":4,"rationale":"Pins the old regex behaviour: for each JS \\s char outside JSON whitespace, a file whose comment line (not first line) is indented with it must parse like the ASCII-indented control. Fails at head today; add to the bdiff data generator too.","refs":[{"id":"pocs/pr6525-comment-indent-whitespace.sh","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2","kind":"requirement"}],"title":"Comment-lines-only Unicode indent partition"},{"forClaim":16,"rationale":"Settles parity of the scanner and console.warn between node and the shell's engine.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":1055},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-3T3F","kind":"requirement"}],"title":"QV4 witness: inline-comment and malformed user extension inside Quickshell"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** omacom/omarchy#6525 (head 913e112d) replaces stripJsonc's line-anchored comment regex with a string-aware scanner, so a `//` comment after content on a line is dropped while `//` inside strings (URLs, after `\\\"`) is kept; the trailing-comma regex pass is unchanged. parseMenuJsonc now logs a console.warn when parsing fails; docs/menu.md and one menu-test.sh hunk follow. Mirror commit dff129dc is the upstream change; later commits are our proof work (witnesses, a pocs tripwire, KI records).\n\n**Is the fix verified?** Yes for its purpose: 16/16 changed decisions covered, 54/54 tests passed and current, and the #13493 corpus inputs go from 0 to 3 rows (bd-05efa2ff, bd-41c905c2, intended). KI-MENU-JSONC-INLINE-COMMENT is fixed; COMMA-IN-STRING, ARRAY-ROOT, UNICODE-WHITESPACE, CR-LINE-ENDINGS, STRIP-GAPS stay open (re-checked).\n\n**Questions for a human.** One real regression, recorded as KI-MENU-JSONC-COMMENT-INDENT-WHITESPACE (cf-39627352): a whole-line comment indented with non-JSON JS whitespace (NBSP, U+3000, VT, FF, U+2028, a BOM after the start) now empties the whole file. Quickshell's FileView drops a LEADING BOM, so a BOM at file start does not trigger it under the shell; the same characters on later lines do. The configured behaviour-diff harness did NOT catch it (its data partition puts the character before every line, so base and head both fail), and compat test_diff did not flag the flipped menu-test.sh witness. Six compatibility changes are unapproved (readiness not_assessed; next decision compat_changes_unapproved, reviewer authority); auditor notes are not approvals. QV4 runtime parity is unobserved.\n\n**Traceability.** 26 requirements code_changed (E4J2 and 3T3F at function level). E4J2's text still says full-line comments. The unmapped pocs script is our KI reproducer, not PR code.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** Effects were not analyzed (effects_unavailable); 14 checks skipped by configuration; live compositor/acceptance tests are in no audit suite."}
